{"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Afluent\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/Afluent\/Sci"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A subject that broadcasts values to multiple consumers without storing a current value.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Unlike ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CurrentValueSubject"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PassthroughSubject"},{"text":" does not retain the most recent value.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"This is an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncSequence"},{"text":" that allows multiple tasks to asynchronously consume values and mimics Combine’s PassthroughSubject.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"final","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PassthroughSubject","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Subscribing","type":"heading","anchor":"Subscribing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A consumer subscribes when its iterator is created, which is when a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for try await"},{"type":"text","text":" loop over the subject"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(or over an operator chain built on it) begins. From then on, every value sent is buffered for that consumer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"until it is consumed, so a consumer that is slower than the sender still sees every value, in order."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Values sent while there are no subscribers are discarded; they are never replayed to a later consumer.","type":"text"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Starting a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" that iterates the subject does not mean it has subscribed yet. If values must"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not be missed, wait until the consumer has subscribed before sending, for example with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"handleEvents(receiveMakeIterator:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"type":"aside","style":"important","name":"Important"},{"level":2,"text":"Example","type":"heading","anchor":"Example"},{"code":["let subject = PassthroughSubject<Int>()","let subscribed = SingleValueSubject<Void>()","","subject.send(0) \/\/ No subscribers yet, so this value is discarded.","","Task {","    for try await value in subject.handleEvents(receiveMakeIterator: { try? subscribed.send() }) {","        print(\"Received value: \\(value)\") \/\/ prints 1, then 2","    }","}","","try await subscribed.execute()","subject.send(1)","subject.send(2)","subject.send(completion: .finished)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PassthroughSubject","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PassthroughSubject","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"PassthroughSubject.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Afluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Afluent\/PassthroughSubject.swift#L41"},"title":"PassthroughSubject","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:7Afluent18PassthroughSubjectC","roleHeading":"Class","symbolKind":"class","modules":[{"name":"Afluent"}]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/afluent\/passthroughsubject"],"traits":[{"interfaceLan